A.2.1 TIER 1 APPROACHES
\par
Approaches for sensitivity analysis in Tier 1 of a PRA are limited to calculations that are based
\par
on changing point estimates. They are generally easy to perform and to communicate. As given by Table
\par
A-1, goals for the sensitivity analysis in Tier 1 include quantifying the relative contributions of the
\par
exposure pathways, identifying potential nonlinear relationships that may exist between input variables
\par
and the risk estimate, and rank ordering the relative contribution of exposure variables to variability or
\par
uncertainty in the risk estimate. This last goal may be the most difficult to achieve due to the limitations
\par
associated with the point estimate methodology. Methods are applied to the hypothetical example
\par
presented above (Section A.2.0) in order to demonstrate the inherent limitations of the Tier 1 approaches
\par
in some situations.
\par
