Together with statistical summaries, graphical data summaries can reveal important characteristics of a
\par
data set, including skewness (asymmetry), number of peaks (multi-modality), behavior in the tails, and
\par
data outliers.
\par
Frequency Distribution or Histogram
\par
The frequency distribution, or histogram, is a graphical approximation of the empirical PDF.
\par
Frequency distributions can be plotted on both linear and log scales. The general strategy for selecting
\par
the number of bins to partition the data is to avoid too much smoothing and too much jaggedness.
\par
