Truncation is typically considered when using unbounded probability distributions (e.g., normal,
\par
lognormal, gamma, Weibull) to characterize variability. Table B-3 gives the theoretical bounds for
\par
selected probability distributions that may be more commonly used in PRA. Truncating the minimum
\par
