\par
The p-value in a statistical test is calculated from a sample and represents the probability of
\par
obtaining a value of the test statistic as extreme or more extreme as the one observed if H0 is in fact true.
\par
When the p-value is small it means either the null hypothesis is not true, or that we have witnessed an
