(e.g., p {$<$} 0.05), the null hypothesis is rejected in favor of the alternative, and we state that the test result is
\par
statistically significant at level ". This does not mean that we have proven Ha is true. Rather, we are
\par
saying that based on our sample results, it is unlikely that H0 is true.
\par
In a GoF test, the hypothesis test is set up the same way as a ``traditional'' hypothesis test, but the
\par
