For example, suppose a model is available to relate soil tetrachlorodibenzodioxin (TCDD)
\par
concentrations at a site with serum concentrations of TCDD. A probability distribution of soil
\par
concentrations is created based upon expert judgment and a limited amount of site specific data. Using
\par
the model, the soil concentrations can be associated with a distribution of serum TCDD concentrations
\par
(P\textregistered ), the prior distribution). New site-specific data (D) are subsequently collected on serum TCDD
\par
concentrations in order to reduce uncertainty in the risk estimate. Assume that it is known that serum
\par
TCDD concentrations generally follow a lognormal distribution and that the best estimate of the
\par
parameters of this distribution come from the prior distribution on serum TCDD. This creates the
\par
