5. DISCUSSION
\par
Our analysis indicates that the expected health
\par
benefits of a Glu-69-based required screening pro-
\par
gram for machinists at typical baseline prevalence
\par
levels far outweigh the expected financial costs for
\par
most health valuations. If an a priori judgment is
\par
made that the qualitative social and ethical risks of
\par
required screening are too burdensome or if required
\par
genetic screening is determined to be illegal,(28) other
\par
Glu-69-based risk management programs may be
\par
