\par
cebo, thereby refuting the null hypothesis.44 But using robust Baye-
\par
sian analysis techniques, Berger demonstrates that the lower bounds
\par
for the percentage of drugs with p-values of 0.05 that are actually inef-
\par
fective is 24\% and the lower bound for the 0.01 group would be about
\par
7\%; the actual values (remembering that the robust Bayesian tech-
\par
niques gives lower bounds) being about 50\% and 15\% respectively.45
\par
As Bayesians are fond of saying, p-values give the right answers to
\par
the wrong questions. When classical statisticians try to bridge the gap
\par
between this right answer to the wrong question (the probability of
