5. Discussion
\par
Our studies suggest that the most accurate way to
\par
obtain a subjective dependence measure is simply to
\par
ask the expert to estimate the correlation between the
\par
two variables in question. The direct assessment of
\par
correlation consistently performed better than any of
\par
the other assessment methods in terms of average
\par
absolute error. R also was judged to be one of the two
\par
easiest assessments to make. In addition, the standard
\par
deviation (of both the equivalent correlations them-
\par
selves as well as the absolute errors) was consistently
\par
less, indicating a greater level of consensus among the
\par
subjects. Finally, in comparison with CF, JP, and
