\par
example of a possible use of the DDN technique
\par
as the supporting technique for an integrated
\par
defence system.
\par
In this sample application, the number of BN in
\par
the inference sub-net will be a function of the
\par
number of tracks/intruders in the controlled
\par
space. The number of nodes in each data fusion
\par
BN will depend upon the number and type of
\par
tracks in the inference sub-net. In addition, the
\par
