\par
\textbf{\emph{3.1.3. Methods}}
\par
\emph{Costs}
\par
The model concentrates upon the differences in variable costs between strategies, because
\par
each option involves an identical environmental setting. The resources involved with each
\par
strategy, in terms of test usage, drugs prescribed and the number of GP visits, are recorded for
\par
each stage of the model for both the UTI and non-UTI branches. The management strategies
\par
are then costed by applying unit costs (Table 2) to the expected resource volumes associated
\par
with each strategy.8
