that the investigators who plan and conduct a study
\par
are generally not the same body as those that make
\par
decisions on the basis of the evidence provided in
\par
part by that study: such decision makers may be
\par
regulatory authorities or healthcare providers. This
\par
division is acknowledged both in the structure of
\par
this report (in which chapter 4 considers design
\par
and monitoring of trials, and chapter 7 examines
\par
decision-making) and in the lower profile given to
\par
decision-making compared with inferences.
