\par
discuss general applications in the health sciences
\par
with an emphasis on decision-making, while
\par
Freedman177 and Lilford and Braunholtz299
\par
concentrate on the ability to combine `objective'
\par
evidence with clinical judgement. Stangl and
\par
Berry426 provide a recent review of biomedical
\par
applications.
\par
There is a huge methodological statistical literature
\par
on general Bayesian methods, much of it quite
\par
