\par
421 (see page 17),
\par
who report the parallel elicitation exercise for
\par
the head-and-neck CHART trial. The prior
\par
distribution, when averaged over the clinicians,
\par
expressed a median anticipated 2 year survival
\par
benefit of 10\%, and a 10\% chance that CHART
\par
would offer no survival benefit at all. When
\par
transformed to a log(hazard ratio) scale, this
\par
subjective prior distribution had a mean of 0.314
\par
(hazard ratio of 1.37) and a precision equivalent
\par
to a trial with 60:40 allocation in which 73
\par
deaths had occurred (50 under CHART, 23
\par
under standard treatment).
\par
3. A sceptical prior was derived using the ideas in
\par
chapter 3: the prior mean is 0 and the precision
\par
is such that the prior probability that the true
\par
benefit exceeds the alternative hypothesis is low
\par
(5\% in this case). This gives a prior equivalent to
\par
trial with 60:40 allocation with 112 events and an
\par
observed log(hazard ratio) of 0.
