\par
without the ISIS-4 data, where p0 is the risk in the
\par
control group at which the treatment has no effect.
\par
The relationship to underlying risk is suggested
\par
before inclusion of ISIS-4, but with a very wide
\par
interval. Nevertheless, the model would have
\par
predicted that the treatment would not be effective
\par
with an underlying risk below 9.1\%. Inclusion of
\par
the ISIS-4 results, whose underlying risk was 7.2\%,
\par
