\textbf{Appendix 2}
\par
Websites and software
\par
Here we provide a selection of sites that
\par
currently provide useful material on Bayesian
\par
methods applicable to health technology assess-
\par
ment and lists of links. This list is not exhaustive
\par
but should provide some entry into the huge range
\par
of material available on the Internet.
\par
This sites below were all functioning in November
\par
2000.
\par
\textbf{Bayesian methods in health}
\par
\textbf{technology assessment}
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.fda.gov/cdrh/}}
\par
This is the home page for the US Food and Drug
\par
Administration's Center for Devices and Radiolog-
\par
ical Health, which contains a number of items
\par
relating to Bayesian methods. To identify these,
\par
use the search facility with the keyword `Bayesian'.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.bayesian-initiative.com/}}
\par
The Bayesian Initiative in Health Economics and
\par
Outcome Research provides useful background
\par
material on Bayesian approaches to pharmaco-
\par
economics, but does not appear to have been
\par
updated for some time.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://omie.med.jhmi.edu/bayes/}}
\par
The Bayesian Communication website is hosted
\par
by Harold Lehmann, and features a prototype
\par
example in which a Bayesian analysis can be
\par
carried out on-line.289--291
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.research.att.com/\textasciitilde volinsky/bma.html}}
\par
The Bayesian Model Averaging web page provides
\par
S-plus and Fortran software for carrying out model
\par
averaging, as well as featuring reprints and links.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.palisade.com/}}
\par
The Palisade Corporation markets the @RISK\textregistered{}
\par
software, which is an add-on to spreadsheet
\par
packages that allows probability distributions to be
\par
placed over the inputs to spreadsheets. Predictive
\par
distributions over the outputs are then obtained by
\par
simulation. Demonstrator versions are available for
\par
downloading.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www-math.bgsu.edu/\textasciitilde albert/mini\_bayes/}}
\par
\textbf{\emph{info.html}}
\par
This site is an adjunct to Jim Albert's book Bayesian
\par
Computation Using Minitab, and features macros for
\par
carrying out a variety of analyses.
\par
\textbf{Bayesian software}
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.shef.ac.uk/\textasciitilde st1ao/1b.html}}
\par
The First Bayes software is freely available, and
\par
features good graphical presentation of conjugate
\par
analysis of basic data sets. It is suitable for teaching,
\par
and is strong on predictive distributions.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.mrc-bsu.cam.ac.uk/bugs/}}
\par
The BUGS software is designed for analysis of
\par
complex analysis using MCMC methods. The
\par
WinBUGS version features an interface for speci-
\par
fying models as graphs. The software assumes
\par
familiarity with Bayesian methods and MCMC
\par
computation.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.epi.mcgill.ca/\textasciitilde web2/Joseph/}}
\par
\textbf{\emph{software.html}}
\par
Lawrence Joseph's Bayesian Software site provides
\par
downloadable code for a wide variety of sample size
\par
calculations using prior opinion.
\par
\textbf{General Bayesian sites}
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://bayes.stat.washington.edu/}}
\par
\textbf{\emph{bayes\_people.html}}
\par
The Bayesian Statistics Personal Web Pages site has
\par
links to the home pages of many researchers in
\par
Bayesian methods. These provide a vast array of
\par
lecture notes, reprints and slide presentations.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.bayesian.org/}}
\par
The International Society for Bayesian Analysis
\par
provides information on its activities and useful
\par
links.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.stat.ucla.edu/\textasciitilde jsanchez/sbssnews/}}
\par
\textbf{\emph{sbssnews.html}}
\par
The American Statistical Association Section on
\par
Bayesian Statistical Sciences (SBSS) has a preprint
\par
archive and links to other sites.
\par
\textbf{\emph{http://www.isds.duke.edu/sites/bayes.html}}
\par
This web page hosted from Duke University
\par
provides a list of Bayesian sites.
