\textbf{6.2.7 Issues arising from the process of monitoring impact}
\par
Detailed observation as carried out by the researcher is clearly not practical
\par
in the normal course of class use of the SLRC but it is a useful tool to gain
\par
evidence of the opportunities for intervention and the processes used by
\par
individual pupils while involved in research activities in the SLRC.
\par
Observation also reveals other things happening in the SLRC which might
\par
not otherwise be noticed, such as how pupils sent from class on an
\par
individual basis cope with the information process considering input from
\par
structured courses and activities.
\par
The observation schedule provided a useful reminder of what to look for but
\par
57proved difficult to complete because of the way the groups were working.
\par
The evaluation given to the pupils by the teacher was felt to be a valuable
\par
tool, providing assessment information on what the pupils had learned about
\par
the topics they researched and about the processes involved and by
\par
providing evaluation information on where adjustments might made to
\par
make the project more effective in future. The questionnaire gave
\par
information about the learning experiences not specifically covered by the
\par
aims of the course but are only a crude indication of what is happening.
\par
Discussion during the class time was difficult between the staff but between
\par
the staff and pupils was both useful in terms of assessing the situations
\par
pupils were facing but also in terms of helping pupils to clarify they tasks.
\par
Logs were kept by the librarians of their observations during the project.
\par
They found it relatively easy, though time-consuming, to consider what was
\par
happening in the SLRC during the project time but less easy to find any
\par
connections beyond this time, i.e. it was not noted when pupils returned to
\par
the SLRC to continue their research. The notes indicated an awareness of
\par
the learning experiences and possible indicators and during the evaluation
\par
of the course with the teacher some of the issues noted were discussed,
\par
suggesting that the reflection provided a useful means of clarifying what
\par
was happening.
