\textbf{Motivation}
\par
{$\bullet$} Observation during the first lesson in the SLRC suggested there was a
\par
good deal of \textbf{\emph{enthusiasm to get started}} and excitement about the
\par
prospect of being in the SLRC. Part of this excitement was due to the
\par
fact that another S2 class was using the SLRC for a home economics
\par
project and friends could get together. However by the end of the first
\par
session in the SLRC, the majority of the pupils had planned their
\par
questions and \textbf{\emph{begun using the resources}}. This class then had a break
\par
from the research for two weeks due to holidays and strike action and
\par
it was noticeable during the next session the pupils were less focused
\par
and more easily distracted. For many of the pupils the enthusiasm
\par
continued to diminish during the subsequent weeks.
\par
\emph{"I enjoy projects and like to be given freedom to research at my pace."}
\par
{$\bullet$} Two girls showed signs of motivation and commitment to the project
\par
when they \textbf{\emph{enquired about taking resources home}} at the end of the
\par
first session but this was not possible because they were needed for
\par
other classes doing the same project. The librarian reported a few
\par
resources were issued during the holiday period but no record was
\par
kept.
\par
{$\bullet$} During the second session, another pupil was \textbf{\emph{keen to show}} the
\par
Researcher the amount of work already accomplished and this
\par
appeared to be of a good standard, including the main requirements of
\par
the project. This pupil was motivated to \textbf{\emph{work at home}} on the project,
