\textbf{6.8.4 Book Week}
\par
\textbf{Background}
\par
The aim of the Book Week is to promote books to the staff and pupils of
\par
the school. The library hosts the events and in the past the librarian has
\par
been instrumental in organising the events. This year, much of the
\par
organisation was carried out by one member of the English department with
\par
support from the librarian and other colleagues.
\par
\textbf{Observation}
\par
Two visiting authors spent a day in the SLRC talking to the English classes.
\par
The English department had wanted the emphasis to be on creative writing
\par
rather than promoting the author's individual work. One author was an
\par
experienced speaker and excellent storyteller and the other was less
\par
experience.
\par
The themes of the craft of writing and getting published were explored and
\par
useful tips and hints were extended to both teachers and pupils. The
\par
audience was felt by one author to be too large and the sessions although
\par
inviting questions were not conducive to pupil interaction.
\par
Another event during the week was a book quiz organised by ten keen S3
\par
pupils for visiting teams of primary 7s. The event was very well organised
\par
and had occupied the S3 pupils for some time.
\par
\textbf{Evidence of Impact}
\par
At the end of one session one \textbf{\emph{pupil asked advice}} from one author about
\par
getting a piece of writing she had done published. Other enquiries were
\par
made about one of the author's published work and whether it was
\par
available in the SLRC \textbf{\emph{to borrow}}. One of the \textbf{\emph{teachers decided to try out an}}
\par
\textbf{\emph{idea}} suggested by one of the authors. The teachers were generally
\par
enthusiastic about visits like this because it allows the pupils to see another
\par
perspective, helps reinforce their teaching, encourages the teachers to
\par
reflect on their teaching.
\par
The teacher felt the pupils who organised the book quiz had gained
\par
\textbf{\emph{experience working as a group}}, it helped give them \textbf{\emph{organisational skills}},
\par
it \textbf{\emph{drew on their knowledge of literature}} and provided a means of giving
\par
them \textbf{\emph{experience of communication in front of an audience}}, which will
\par
become part of the 5-14, level F curriculum. The pupils themselves felt they
\par
had learned organisational, team and time management skills, and they had
\par
to think about their reading and knowledge of books.
