\textbf{6.8.6 Discussion}
\par
The idea of special events is to motivate pupils and stimulate interest and
\par
this is achieved in very subtle ways; the impact is on individual pupils and
\par
in a way that is often not noticed or recognised within the school.
\par
Sometimes it reflects impact from an activity carried out in the past.
\par
In the same way ad hoc use of the SLRC is very individual and the
\par
reinforcement or acquisition of new skills and knowledge often goes
\par
unnoticed.
\par
During the school visits the Researcher observed or was made aware of
\par
numerous incidences where the SLRC had made an impact in a small way
\par
to the attitude or the learning experience of individual pupils.
