\textbf{INTERVIEW WITH TEACHER}
\par
Introduction: this research is looking at the impact of the school library resource centre
\par
(SLRC) on learning.
\par
Would like to ask you a few questions before you use the SLRC, and again after your use. We
\par
would appreciate any thoughts you may have during use and this could be noted on the
\par
sheet/book.
\par
During this piece of work it would be helpful for our research if the pupils write all their work
\par
in jotters (or on paper) which is kept and studied along with the final product at the end of the
\par
project. We would appreciate the opportunity to study the work in progress and the final
\par
product for evidence of the impact of the SLRC on learning.
\par
At the end of the project we would like to pupils to complete a simple questionnaire to
\par
investigate how they feel the use of the SLRC may have had an impact.
\par
1. What are your priorities for this piece of work?
\par
2. Why did you decide to do this piece of work using the school library?
\par
3. How would you have approached the same piece of work if the school library had not
\par
been available?
\par
{$\bullet$} Would you have expected the same outcomes?
\par
{$\bullet$} Would you have been looking for different things during the process and in the end
\par
product?
\par
{$\bullet$} How would the pupils gained the skills expected from using the school library?
\par
4. In what ways do you expect using the school library to help (impact on) the pupils'
\par
learning from the point of view of the curriculum?
\par
5. Do you expect using the school library to help their learning in ways that are not directly
\par
related to the curriculum subject? How or in what ways?
\par
6. How would you look for evidence of the school library's contribution to their learning?
\par
7. Will you be looking for evidence of their learning from the school library?
\par
8. How will using the school library in this instance help you either as a teacher or
\par
personally?
\par
9. Do you feel the use of the school library was successful in fulfilling your reasons for
\par
using it?
\par
10. Did you notice any unexpected events which might/would have had an impact on
\par
learning?
\par
11. Did you feel your major input in the school library was directed towards your intended
\par
priorities? If not, where was your input directed?
\par
12. Please state your priorities and rate them on a scale of 1-10 (1 = trivial, 10 = vital), then
\par
state your inputs and rate them, and then state the outcomes and rate them.\textbf{Appendix 8}
