6.2. LOW-COST OPTIONS
\par
A low-cost simulation is presented for the CDM region by assuming that investors
\par
will only be interested in projects with emission reduction costs lower than a certain
\par
critical level of, say, 100 \$/Mg CO2-eq. We have chosen this (somewhat arbitrary)
\par
level, because a lower level would exclude too many projects from the analysis,
\par
thereby diminishing its robustness, whereas a higher level would be rather unlikely
\par
given the potential presence of alternative and cheaper investment options in devel-140 EDWIN WOERDMAN AND WYTZE VAN DER GAAST
