4. Observation task evaluation
\par
Specification of importance (priorities) of different
\par
observation tasks, based on the current tactical situa-
\par
tion, is significant to adapt sensor operations to chang-
\par
ing environments. Information about task priorities can
\par
be very useful in scheduling sensor actions and for ne-
\par
gotiation among sensors in a decentralized architecture.
\par
4.1. Evaluation based on fuzzy decision trees
\par
Molina Lopez et al. [53] developed a symbolic rea-
\par
soning process to infer numeric evaluations of defense
\par
surveillance tasks using fuzzy decision trees. Each node
\par
in the decision tree is a linguistic variable with its pos-
\par
