6.1. Search-based approaches to sensor selection
\par
The selection of a sensor subset to be applied to a
\par
given task can be considered as a search problem in
\par
combinatorial space. The goal is to find the most ap-
\par
propriate solution among all possible sensor combina-
\par
tions. Hence a key point involved is how to evaluate
\par
trials in the problem space.
\par
Sensors'suitabilitywasassessedin[25]usingfuzzyset
\par
