\par
which the best sensor subset for a given task can be
\par
explored. Molina Lopez et al. [52] introduced some
\par
heuristics to be associated with nodes of the search tree
\par
for sensor subset evaluation in terms of sensor load and
\par
sensor suitability. The sensor load constitutes an esti-
\par
mate of the sensor resources required to accomplish a
\par
task, while the sensor's suitability to perform a task is
\par
definedasafunctionofthenecessityoffulfillingthetask
\par
and the ability of the sensor to perform it. The objective
\par
function for a search algorithm should be constructed in
\par
a proper manner to reflect a good balance between the
\par
two factors.
