plementation details but pointed out that decision the-
\par
ory itself does not constitute a solution to the problem.
\par
6.4. Fuzzy logic resource manager
\par
Gonsalves and Rinkus [26] described an intelligent
\par
fusion and asset management processor with its fourth
\par
level being a fuzzy logic collection manager, which is
\par
responsible for mapping the current situation state and
\par
enemy track information into (job) requests on sensing
\par
assets. The mapping depends on prior knowledge of
\par
sensor capabilities and enemy tactical doctrine. How-
\par
ever, this paper does not explain how to incorporate
\par
fuzzy logic in the knowledge representation and rea-
\par
soning.
\par
Asomewhatsimilarwork tothat ofGonsalves, called
\par
fuzzy-logic based resource manager, was presented in[65]
\par
which aims at optimal allocation of various resources
\par
distributed over many dissimilar platforms. A fuzzy
\par
decision tree for resource management was constructed
\par
via codifying related military expertise, with parameters
\par
of root concept membership functions being optimized
\par
by a genetic algorithm. The fitness function for the
\par
genetic algorithm was established based upon various
\par
considerations of geometry, physics, engineering and
\par
military doctrine. A later paper [66] by the same authors
\par
extends the idea of the former paper [65] by incorpo-
\par
rating data mining techniques [6], which are generally
\par
understood as efficient discovery of valuable, implicit
\par
knowledge and information from a large collection of
\par
data, for performance optimization of the fuzzy decision
\par
tree.Inparticular,ageneticalgorithmwasappliedinthe
\par
data mining process to yield parameters of the root
\par
conceptmembershipfunctionsbaseduponadatabaseof
\par
scenarios. Two possible ways to construct a database of
\par
good quality were discussed. A comprehensive scenario
\par
database is beneficial for the data mining technique to
\par
extract knowledge covering a wide range of behaviors
\par
and providing robust strategies to resource allocation.
\par
Otherwise a small data set containing a narrow spec-
\par
trum of scenarios could result in a resource manager
\par
effective in some cases but ineffective in others.
